> **عربي:** قسم — 3) Real IDE LSP for TypeScript

### 3) Real IDE LSP for TypeScript
**Why:** Agent LSP-lite ≠ IDE language service. Heavy refactors need F12 / refs / rename / diagnostics that match `tsconfig`.  
**Note:** Strengthens desktop Execute quality after Plan / Cloud handoff.

- [ ] Go to Definition (F12) from Monaco using project TS service / language graph bridge
- [ ] Find All References (Shift+F12) in editor UI (peek or panel)
- [ ] Rename Symbol (workspace-aware, at least TS/TSX)
- [ ] Diagnostics: keep Problems panel + agent awareness in sync after edits
- [ ] Prefer open-tab + import-neighborhood models over blind “load N files”
- [ ] Optional: wire agent `find_definition` results to “Open at line” consistently
- [ ] Tests: selection → def path; rename dry-run or fixture project

**Exit criteria:** On a multi-file TS fixture, F12 and refs work without opening chat; rename updates imports; tests green.

> **عربي:** قسم — 4) Monorepo performance & context budgets

### 4) Monorepo performance & context budgets
**Why:** Index + chat history must stay usable at 10k–50k files. Helps Plan Mode grounding on huge repos too.

- [ ] Index size budgets (max files/chunks configurable; streaming/jsonl if JSON gets huge)
- [ ] Search timeouts / early-exit budgets in `search_codebase` / `parallel_investigate`
- [ ] Compaction settings (recent count / max chars) exposed in agent settings
- [ ] Avoid full re-embed of entire corpus on tiny upserts (already partial — audit at scale)
- [ ] Progress UI while first deep index builds on huge repos
- [ ] Fixture or bench notes for “large repo” smoke (even if synthetic)

**Exit criteria:** Opening a large workspace doesn’t freeze UI; search returns within a bounded time; settings persist.

> **عربي:** قسم — 5) Deeper semantics (optional model embeddings, still local-first)

### 5) Deeper semantics (optional model embeddings, still local-first)
**Why:** Hashed embeddings help; real local vectors close more “concept search” gaps.

- [ ] Optional local embedding backend (e.g. transformers.js / sidecar model) behind a flag
- [ ] Keep BM25+hash hybrid as default (no mandatory download)
- [ ] Evaluate Gemini embeddings only as **opt-in** (not default — local-first)
- [ ] Quality tests: synonym/topic queries beat BM25-only baseline on fixtures

**Exit criteria:** Flag off = current behavior; flag on = measurable relevance gain on fixtures.

> **عربي:** قسم — 6) Productize PR → CI → Fix

### 6) Productize PR → CI → Fix
**Why:** Tools exist; the loop should feel like a first-class workflow (and pair with Plan Mode ops steps).

- [ ] Clear chat/SCM affordance: “Push & watch CI” / failure checklist UI
- [ ] Auto-suggest next fix step when checks fail (without silent force-push)
- [ ] Draft PR template from plan + changed files
- [ ] Tests for CI parse / failure line extraction

**Exit criteria:** User can run push→checks→fix→recheck without leaving Vigil.

